    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0240" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.003 Wallace, Henry A./49</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice President Wallace to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-25">April 25, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Secretary Hull</hi>: As you know, I am planning
                    to leave shortly for the Far East and in view of the rapidly approaching date of
                    my departure I am finding it necessary to complete all plans.</p>
                <p>Because of the prime necessity of being in close touch with the State
                    Department’s policies and procedures, I should appreciate it if you could find
                    it possible to assign Mr. John Carter Vincent as a member of my party. Besides
                    relying on him in the course of the journey I could then count on him to see
                    that all necessary details of planning within his sphere of activity are covered
                    in advance of departure.</p>
                <p>I want you to know how deeply I appreciate the fine cooperation I have received
                    from the people of your Department, and particularly from Mr. Ballantine, Mr.
                    Bohlen and Mr. Vincent.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
